1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,840
Cut here.

2
00:00:01,300 --> 00:00:02,200
Tear up here.

3
00:00:02,820 --> 00:00:04,155
How does an onion reach your

4
00:00:04,180 --> 00:00:04,660
eyes?

5
00:00:05,270 --> 00:00:07,270
The knife damages the onion's tissue,

6
00:00:07,570 --> 00:00:09,330
starting a chain of chemical reactions.

7
00:00:10,050 --> 00:00:11,925
One step uses an enzyme called

8
00:00:11,950 --> 00:00:14,030
lachrymatory factor synthase.

9
00:00:14,530 --> 00:00:16,345
It helps make a volatile compound

10
00:00:16,370 --> 00:00:18,030
called the lachrymatory factor.

11
00:00:18,730 --> 00:00:20,305
Volatile means it can enter the

12
00:00:20,330 --> 00:00:20,710
air.

13
00:00:21,410 --> 00:00:23,745
That compound causes the familiar eye

14
00:00:23,770 --> 00:00:26,130
irritation associated with chopping onions.

15
00:00:26,580 --> 00:00:28,675
So the slice and the irritation

16
00:00:28,700 --> 00:00:30,440
happen in different places,

17
00:00:30,780 --> 00:00:32,680
connected by an airborne chemical.

18
00:00:33,660 --> 00:00:35,360
The knife never touched your eye,

19
00:00:35,700 --> 00:00:37,315
it started a reaction that could

20
00:00:37,340 --> 00:00:37,900
reach it.
